---
// FRT-30: Privacy Policy route on the shared foundations (BaseLayout supplies the
// document shell, skip link, nav, and the footer link that points here). The page is
// static prose; no island, no client script. Content follows the legal-tos-privacy
// skill audit: public game data, optional account features, and technical data.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How SPT Leaderboard collects, uses, shares, and keeps data: public game statistics from the mod, optional account features, cookies, retention, and your choices."
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><strong>Last updated: October 11, 2026</strong></p>
  <p>
    This page explains what data the SPT Leaderboard website and service handle, why we handle
    it, and what choices you have. Read it together with our Terms of Service.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    SPT Leaderboard is run by the SPT Leaderboard team. We run this website, the leaderboard
    service behind it, and the SPT Leaderboard mod that sends game statistics to that service.
    This policy covers all three.
  </p>

  <h2>What data we handle</h2>
  <p>We handle four kinds of data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>public game statistics that the mod sends to us</li>
    <li>account details that you choose to add when you log in</li>
    <li>technical data that the site needs to work and to stay secure</li>
    <li>a few display choices that stay in your browser</li>
  </ul>
  <table class="privacy-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Data</th>
        <th scope="col">Examples</th>
        <th scope="col">Where it comes from</th>
        <th scope="col">Who can see it</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Public game statistics</th>
        <td>Rank, score, level, K/D, raids, kills, survival rate, play time, achievements, trader and hideout progress</td>
        <td>The SPT Leaderboard mod, during game sessions</td>
        <td>Everyone, on the leaderboard and your profile</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Equipment and weapon data</th>
        <td>Gear, weapon attachments, Stattrack weapon statistics</td>
        <td>The SPT Leaderboard mod</td>
        <td>Everyone, on your profile and in Weapon Meta</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Online status</th>
        <td>Whether you are online, your in-stash or in-raid state, the map and side during a raid, the in-raid game time</td>
        <td>Heartbeats from the mod, while you play</td>
        <td>Everyone, as an online marker</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Profile details you add</th>
        <td>Profile picture, About Me text, Discord name, profile style choices</td>
        <td>You, through your profile settings</td>
        <td>Everyone who views your profile</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Comments, replies, and likes</th>
        <td>The comments you write on a profile, your replies, your likes, and the time you posted</td>
        <td>You</td>
        <td>Everyone who views the profile where you posted</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Friends</th>
        <td>Friend requests you send or receive, and friend status between two accounts</td>
        <td>You</td>
        <td>You, and the other account in the friend relation</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Login session</th>
        <td>A session cookie, your login state, your username, your avatar, your unread notification count</td>
        <td>The login service, when you log in</td>
        <td>You, in your own browser</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Technical data</th>
        <td>IP address, browser type, the pages and requests your browser makes</td>
        <td>Your browser, our servers, and our hosting provider</td>
        <td>Our team and the providers that run the service</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Display choices</th>
        <td>Sort order of the leaderboard, whether auto-update is on</td>
        <td>Your browser</td>
        <td>Only your browser; we do not receive it</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>What is public by design</h2>
  <p>
    A leaderboard only works when its results are public. So most game data that the mod sends
    is public. Anyone who visits the site can see:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>your player name and team tag</li>
    <li>your rank, score, level, K/D, raids, kills, survival rate, and play time</li>
    <li>your achievements, trader progress, and other profile progress</li>
    <li>your equipment and weapon statistics</li>
    <li>your profile picture, and any About Me text or Discord name that you set</li>
    <li>the comments and likes on your profile</li>
    <li>whether you are online, and what you are doing in a raid, while you play with the mod</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The mod sends more game data to our servers than the site shows today. Some of that data is
    not shown on the site.
  </p>

  <h2>What only logged-in users can do</h2>
  <p>
    Some features need you to log in. You need to be logged in to write comments, reply, like,
    add friends, see your friend requests and friend status, change your profile details, and
    see your unread notification count. Logging in uses the account login service. This website
    does not store your password.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>We use as few cookies as we can.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Login session cookie.</strong> The login service sets this cookie when you log in.
      It tells our servers that your browser is logged in. It is needed for the login features.
      Log out to end your session in this browser.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local storage.</strong> The site saves two display choices in your browser: your
      leaderboard sort order and whether auto-update is on. This data stays on your device. We do
      not send it to our servers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No tracking.</strong> This site does not use analytics tools, advertising cookies,
      or third-party trackers.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use your data and why</h2>
  <p>
    We use each kind of data for a specific purpose. Under the GDPR, we name a legal basis for each
    purpose. These are our bases:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Public game statistics and the leaderboard:</strong> our legitimate interest in
      running a public ranking of game results. You control this by deciding whether to run the mod.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Profile details, comments, and friends:</strong> the contract to provide the features
      that you choose to use. You control this by choosing whether to use them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Login session:</strong> the contract to provide login, and our legitimate interest in
      keeping accounts secure.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Online status:</strong> our legitimate interest in showing who is playing live. You
      control this by deciding whether to run the mod.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Security and reliability:</strong> our legitimate interest in keeping the service up
      and protected from abuse.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Display choices:</strong> we do not process these. They stay in your browser.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal data. We do not use your data for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
  <p>
    We share data only with the service providers that run the site, and when the law requires it.
    Public data is visible to everyone, as described above.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting:</strong> our hosting provider receives the web requests your browser makes,
      including your IP address, so that it can deliver the site.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Item image CDN:</strong> weapon and item icons load from the tarkov.dev image server
      (assets.tarkov.dev). Your browser asks that server for each icon, so the server receives your
      IP address and the item it is asked for. We do not control how that service handles data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Discord and GitHub:</strong> the footer and this page link to them. Nothing is sent to
      them when this page loads. If you follow a link, that service's own privacy terms apply.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>
    The operators of the leaderboard decide how long each kind of data is kept. Ask the moderators
    for the current rule if you need it.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Season results:</strong> each season is kept as a record. Past seasons stay visible in
      places such as Global Insights and the past season winners.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Profile details, comments, and friend data:</strong> kept while your account is active.
      After that, the operators decide.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Login session:</strong> until you log out or the session expires.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Online status:</strong> you count as online for 5 minutes after your last heartbeat.
      How long heartbeat records are stored on the server is described in the backend documentation
      (see <a href="#server-data">Server data</a>).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Display choices:</strong> until you clear your browser's site data.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We limit access to data to the people who need it to run the service. We take reasonable steps
    to protect the data we hold. No online system is perfectly secure, so we cannot promise that
    your data will never be exposed. If a breach affects your data, we will tell you as the law
    requires.
  </p>

  <h2>Where data is processed</h2>
  <p>
    Our hosting providers and our backend service may run in countries other than yours. When data
    moves to another country, this policy still applies to it. Where the law requires extra
    safeguards for a transfer, we will put them in place.
  </p>

  <h2 id="server-data">Server data</h2>
  <p>
    The backend service documents how server logs, data storage, and retention work in detail.
    A link to that documentation is pending and will be added to this page when it is published.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights and choices</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have these rights over your data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access:</strong> ask for a copy of the data we hold about you.</li>
    <li><strong>Correction:</strong> ask us to fix data that is wrong.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Deletion:</strong> ask us to delete your data. Some season results may stay in the
      leaderboard history. If we cannot remove something, we will tell you why.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Restriction and objection:</strong> ask us to limit how we use your data, or object to a
      use that is based on our legitimate interests.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Portability:</strong> ask for your data in a common, machine-readable format.</li>
    <li><strong>Withdrawing consent:</strong> withdraw any consent you gave, where we rely on consent.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Complaint:</strong> complain to your local data protection authority.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To use these rights, contact the moderators on Discord (see <a href="#contact">Contact</a>).
    We may ask you to confirm who you are before we act on a request. We aim to answer within
    30 days.
  </p>
  <h3>Your choices</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Do not use the mod if you do not want your game data to appear on the leaderboard. You can
      uninstall the mod, or disconnect the service from the F12 BepInEx menu.
    </li>
    <li>Log out to end your login session in this browser.</li>
    <li>Clear your browser's site data to remove the display choices stored there.</li>
    <li>Contact the moderators about any of your data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website and the leaderboard are not made for children under 16. We do not knowingly collect
    data from children under 16. If you think a child has sent us data, contact the moderators on
    Discord, and we will remove it as far as we can.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. When we do, we will change the date at the top of this page. For
    major changes, we will post a notice on this site before the change takes effect. If you keep
    using the service after a change, the updated policy applies to you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions or requests about your data, contact the moderators of the SPT Leaderboard on
    Discord:
    <a href="https://discord.gg/UrRkqwdgnd" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SPT Leaderboard Discord</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

